From fcc20ae741cee8c66aae9a5b41e49f97d1a3f543 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikita Shliakov <profinch@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 23:51:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] metal: a load limit, MXBM_METAL_LOAD=1..100

Below 100 every round launches fewer threadgroups and each one loops over
its share of the buckets (gtotal, threadgroups_per_grid), so fewer GPU
cores run at once and the GPU draws less power; the solve takes longer
rather than the solver pausing between solves. At 100 the launch is the
full grid as before. MXBM_METAL_LOAD_FILE names a file holding the number,
re-read before every solve, so a front end can move the limit while mining;
MXBM_METAL_SLOTS sets the threadgroups in flight directly, for tuning.

The table of threadgroups per load step was measured on an M5 Pro
(16 cores) and scales by core count elsewhere:

  load   sol/s   GPU W        load   sol/s   GPU W
  100%   10.5    19.6          50%    5.2    11.1
   90%    9.6    18.8          40%    4.3     9.5
   80%    8.6    17.5          30%    3.1     7.5
   70%    7.6    14.9          20%    2.2     5.8
   60%    6.5    12.8          10%    0.9     3.7

test_metal_solver (the KAT goldens) passes at every load.
---
 kernels/metal/entry.metal            |   9 +-
 kernels/metal/fused_round.metal      | 126 ++++++++++++++++---------
 kernels/metal/pipeline_kernels.metal | 134 ++++++++++++++-------------
 src/gpu/metal_solver.mm              |  70 ++++++++++++--
 4 files changed, 222 insertions(+), 117 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernels/metal/entry.metal b/kernels/metal/entry.metal
index e8ee6ee..42b1eff 100644
--- a/kernels/metal/entry.metal
+++ b/kernels/metal/entry.metal
@@ -52,8 +52,11 @@ kernel void entry_scatter(const device uint64_t* pp4      [[buffer(0)]],
                           device atomic_uint*    counts   [[buffer(5)]],
                           device uint64_t*       belem    [[buffer(6)]],
                           device atomic_uint*    drops    [[buffer(7)]],
-                          uint g [[thread_position_in_grid]])
+                          uint g0    [[thread_position_in_grid]],
+                          uint gridN [[threads_per_grid]])
 {
-    if (g >= count) return;
-    mxbm::metalk::entry_body(begin + g, pp4, bkt_bits, bkt_cap, counts, belem, drops);
+    // Load limit: the host may launch fewer threads than elements; each then takes
+    // every gridN-th element.
+    for (uint g = g0; g < count; g += gridN)
+        mxbm::metalk::entry_body(begin + g, pp4, bkt_bits, bkt_cap, counts, belem, drops);
 }
